doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23969070"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23969070"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  MeshStack is the distributed-inference layer for the THOX device
  family: a private household mesh of small computers that pool memory
  and compute for local-first AI. This report reconciles two design
  lineages (storage-aware parallelism; pipeline sharding with a KV
  graph and a secrets grant graph) and the Auto Device Role Mode lease
  design into one priced, grant-gated, lease-fenced system. Pipeline
  stage placement is priced against each node's storage and RAM floors;
  KV cache moves between nodes only under an explicit grant; device
  roles are held under lease fencing so a departed holder cannot act on
  a stale authorisation. Evidence is classed measured (named general
  host classes), calculated (public device floors), or simulated
  (protocol logic); no THOX device measurement is claimed. Edition
  v1.1.0 (evidence edition) headline results: lossless compression of
  real GGUF KV (f16) is 1.17 to 1.20x with the byte-split zstd codec,
  bit-exact (the v1.0.1 figure of 1.512x was a bfloat16-tensor result
  and is restated); HMAC chunk keying 9.67 microseconds per 64-token
  chunk; the measured 27B state geometry is 65,536 B/token of attention
  KV plus a fixed 156,894,356 B recurrent state per sequence, and at
  public floors an Air+Mini+Clip trio still cannot place the 27.8B
  reference model (12 GB trio floor vs 14.6 GiB Q4 weights) and is
  returned Unplaceable; the measured PLACE transfer overhead is
  a = 0.196 s with crossovers at 13.2 tokens (P50) and 40.8 (P100) and
  none at P200 or above, and the 65536-token transfer was not
  completed; a live fencing drill on the deployed coordinator accepted
  zero stale authorisations after a lease re-grant (15 to 16); a
  two-host llama.cpp split generated 2.3 tok/s at n = 1 with transport
  caveats stated, and the 27B split was not achieved.
keywords:
  - MeshStack
  - ThoxOS
  - pipeline parallelism
